e effective date.","For this proposal, retention in the existing approval process excludes the pending application from the new removal of prior approval.","The stated home-supervision rationale does not add a distinct approval or supervision test to item (ii)'s express home-jurisdiction compliance condition.","The absent FAQs may qualify implementation; this is a reading of the supplied text only."],"citations":[{"quote":"The key streamlined measures cover the following post-authorisation matters:","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u3.575"},{"quote":"Removing the SFC’s requirement on prior approval for material changes in investment objectives, policies and restrictions which comply with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, except for changes that involve novel or complex product features and/or which may have local policy implications.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u5.840"},{"quote":"1 For this circular, UCITS funds means (i) Undertakings for Collective Investment in Transferable Securities (UCITS) domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland and the Netherlands, and (ii) collective investment schemes domiciled in the United Kingdom authorised as UK UCITS.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"},{"quote":"The streamlined measures set out in the relevant FAQs will take effect on 28 November 2025 (Effective Date).","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"},{"quote":"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will be processed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"},{"quote":"The SFC will continue to conduct post-vetting of scheme changes (including those not subject to the SFC’s prior approval) and related revised documents filed with the SFC.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"}],"distinction":"This reading tests eligibility for the selected removal of prior approval. The strongest unresolved alternative concerns pending application