ocessed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"},{"quote":"The SFC will continue to conduct post-vetting of scheme changes (including those not subject to the SFC’s prior approval) and related revised documents filed with the SFC.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"}],"distinction":"This reading treats item (ii) as conditional withdrawal of prior approval. A qualifying change receives that relief; an excluded change remains subject to the applicable existing rules, whose exact duty is unavailable. The strongest uncertainty is the transition: its wording expressly preserves application processing but does not resolve withdrawal and resubmission. The packet supports this reading with unresolved questions more strongly than a second complete approval rule.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The fund is either a UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands, or a UK-domiciled collective investment scheme authorised as UK UCITS.","name":"covered_ucits","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The selected change is a post-authorisation material change to the fund's investment objective, policy or restriction.","name":"covered_material_change","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u3.575","d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"Date for which availability of the circular's approval relief is being assessed; selection of the legally relevant event date remains subject to clarification.","name":"assessment_date","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"The selected change complies with the applicable requirements of the fund's home jurisdiction.","name":"home_requirements_met","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"